re are no signs of progression or complications. \n\nP: Maintain current treatment with hydrocortisone 10 mg daily. Schedule a return visit in 3-6 months for ongoing monitoring. \n\n--- 08/02/2023 Office Visit --- \nS: Mr. Bryant presents for follow-up of his adrenal insufficiency caused by a pituitary adenoma. He reports feeling stable with no recent episodes of weakness or fatigue. He has been taking hydrocortisone 10 mg daily as prescribed. There are no new symptoms of adrenal insufficiency or any recent illnesses. \n\nO: Vital signs are stable with a blood pressure of 128/79 mmHg a"
